# Implementation Plan - VoNR Coverage Section Layout Update

Modify the VoNR coverage section to arrange three key metric charts (RSRP, SINR, and TxPower) vertically for each run and reduce their size.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component Name] CoveragePerformance

#### [MODIFY] [VonrTimeLineChart.js](file:///d:/ReportGenerator/report-generator-app/src/ReportDetails/CoveragePerformance/VonrTimeLineChart.js)
- Update the component to accept `height` and `width` props.
- Use these props in the container div style.
- Default `height` to `300px` and `width` to `100%` to maintain compatibility with other uses if any.

#### [MODIFY] [VonrCoverageSection.js](file:///d:/ReportGenerator/report-generator-app/src/ReportDetails/CoveragePerformance/VonrCoverageSection.js)
- Reorganize the "TimeLine Analysis" sections.
- For each run, display RSRP, SINR, and TxPower charts vertically.
- Pass reduced `height` (e.g., `220px`) and `width` (e.g., `90%`) to [VonrTimeLineChart](file:///d:/ReportGenerator/report-generator-app/src/ReportDetails/CoveragePerformance/VonrTimeLineChart.js#24-170).
- Ensure appropriate headers and `PageBreak` usage to keep runs separated if needed, or group them logically.
- **Clarification**: I will confirm if the user wants exactly 3 runs or if "Three TimelineCharts" refers to the 3 metrics. Based on the "vertical arrangement" request, grouping by metric (RSRP, SINR, TxPower) for each run seems most likely.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- None available for UI layout.

### Manual Verification
